(449, 1, '2025-06-24 23:50:38', '2025-06-24 23:50:38', '<p>Prosthetics have come a long way—from wooden pegs to advanced cybernetic limbs that do more than restore function—they <strong data-start=\"243\" data-end=\"254\">enhance</strong> it.</p>		\n					<h2>The Journey</h2>				\n		<p data-start=\"1477\" data-end=\"1638\">Connected implants may be <strong data-start=\"698\" data-end=\"708\">hacked</strong>, leading to loss of control, surveillance, or even bodily harm. Bio-firewalls and quantum encryption are essential, but no system is flawless.</p><p><strong data-start=\"279\" data-end=\"301\">1. Early prosthetics:</strong> Simple wooden or metal tools for basic use.</p><p><strong data-start=\"350\" data-end=\"371\">2. Mechanical limbs:</strong> Used cables and joints for movement.</p><p><strong data-start=\"279\" data-end=\"301\">3. </strong><strong data-start=\"413\" data-end=\"435\">Myoelectric limbs:</strong> Controlled by muscle signals for intuitive use.</p><p><strong data-start=\"279\" data-end=\"301\">4. </strong><strong data-start=\"488\" data-end=\"518\">Neural-linked cybernetics:</strong> Today’s limbs connect directly to the nervous system, providing movement and even sensory feedback.</p>		\n					<h2>Today’s Cyber-Limbs</h2>				\n		<p data-start=\"647\" data-end=\"667\"><em>AI-driven movement</em></p><p data-start=\"670\" data-end=\"698\"><em>Realistic tactile feedback</em></p><p data-start=\"701\" data-end=\"733\"><em>Lightweight, durable materials</em></p><p><em>Adaptive learning software</em></p>', 'From Organic to Mechanical: The Evolution of Cybernetic Limbs', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '222-revision-v1', '', '', '2025-06-24 23:50:38', '2025-06-24 23:50:38', '', 222, 'http://localhost/futurionix/?p=449', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
